DAX Implementation Guide


1. Revenue Measures
-- Basic revenue calculation
Total Revenue = 
CALCULATE(
    SUM(Orders[TotalAmount]),
    Orders[OrderStatus] = "Completed"
)

Logic:

Sums all order amounts
Filters to completed orders only
Used in all revenue visuals



2. Count Measures
dax
-- Count distinct orders
Total Orders = COUNTA(Orders[OrderID])

-- Count unique customers
Total Customers = DISTINCTCOUNT(Orders[CustomerID])

-- Count returns
Total Returns = COUNTA(Returns[ReturnID])

Logic:

COUNTA counts non-blank cells
DISTINCTCOUNT counts unique values
Used for volume metrics



3. Average/Rate Measures
dax
-- Calculate average per order
Avg Order Value = 
CALCULATE(
    AVERAGE(Orders[TotalAmount]),
    Orders[OrderStatus] = "Completed"
)

-- Calculate return percentage
Return Rate % = 
DIVIDE(
    COUNTA(Returns[ReturnID]),
    CALCULATE(COUNTA(Orders[OrderID]), Orders[OrderStatus] = "Completed")
) * 100

Logic:

AVERAGE calculates mean values
DIVIDE handles division with 0 protection
Multiplied by 100 for percentage display



4. Category Analysis Measures
dax
-- Revenue by category (works with category filter)
Category Revenue = 
CALCULATE(
    SUM(Orders[TotalAmount]),
    Orders[OrderStatus] = "Completed"
)

-- Products sold by category
Category Products Sold = 
SUMX(OrderDetails, OrderDetails[Quantity])

Logic:

CALCULATE respects category context
SUMX iterates through rows
Aggregates based on current filter context


5. Growth Measures
dax
-- Month-over-Month comparison
MoM Growth % = 
DIVIDE(
    [Total Revenue],
    CALCULATE([Total Revenue], DATEADD(Orders[OrderDate], -1, MONTH))
) * 100 - 100

-- Year-over-Year comparison
YoY Growth % = 
DIVIDE(
    [Total Revenue],
    CALCULATE([Total Revenue], DATEADD(Orders[OrderDate], -1, YEAR))
) * 100 - 100

Logic:

DATEADD shifts dates for comparison
Subtracting 100 converts ratio to percentage change
